   "source": [
    "KNN (K-Nearest Neighbors) \n",
    "KNN stands for K-Nearest Neighbors. It is a supervised Machine Learning algorithm used for both classification and regression.\n",
    "\n",
    "It predicts the output of a new data point by looking at the closest existing data points (neighbors).\n",
    "What is K in KNN?\n",
    "K represents the number of nearest neighbors considered for prediction.\n",
    "Suppose K = 3.\n",
    "    The three nearest students have these results:\n",
    "Neighbor\tResult\n",
    "Student A\tPass\n",
    "Student B\tPass\n",
    "Student C\tFail\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "- Pass = 2 votes\n",
    "- Fail = 1 vote\n",
    "Therefore, the new student is predicted as Pass.This is called majority voting.\n",
    "How does KNN calculate distance?\n",
    "KNN commonly uses Euclidean Distance.\n",
    "\n",
    "d = sqrt((x2-x1)^2+(y2-y1)^2)\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "Consider two students:\n",
    "               X                 Y\n",
    "- Student A: Study hours = 4, Attendance = 80\n",
    "- Student B: Study hours = 5, Attendance = 85\n",
    "                         d=sqrt((5-4)^2+(85-80)^2) = sqrt((1)+(25)) = 5.10\n",
    "KNN calculates distances between the new data point and existing data points to identify the nearest neighbors.\n",
    "Types of KNN\n",
    "Type\t                   Purpose\t                                      Example\n",
    "KNN Classification\t  Predicts a category or class.\t                    Pass / Fail\n",
    "KNN Regression\t      Predicts a numerical value.\t                    Predicting house prices.\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "If there is a tie up, if k=4, pass=2, fail=2.........\n",
    "In this situation, Scikit-learn's default KNN classifier uses a tie-breaking rule based on class \n",
    "ordering (for a binary classification with equally weighted neighbours, the class with the smaller encoded label is selected).\n",
    "[ if fail=0 and pass=1, smaller encoded value will be 0 so it will predicted as 0]\n",
    "    \n",
    "Advantages and disadvantages\n",
    "Advantages\t                                           Disadvantages\n",
    "Easy to understand.\t                        Prediction can be slow for large datasets.\n",
    "Simple to implement.\t                    Sensitive to irrelevant features.\n",
    "No complex training process.\t            Affected by different feature scales.\n",
    "Supports classification and regression.\t    Choosing the correct K is important.\n",
    "\n",
    "KeyPoints:\n",
    "KNN is a supervised learning algorithm.\n",
    "It is a distance-based algorithm.\n",
    "It supports classification and regression.\n",
    "Feature scaling is important because distance calculations are used.\n",
    "Selecting the correct K value affects prediction performance.\n",
    "\n",
    "KNN is called as a Lazy Learning Algorithm --->Because it does not perform much computation during training. It stores the data and performs most of the calculations when a new prediction is requested."
   ]
  }
